       # type: (Dict[str, str]) -> Dict[str, str]
       reveal_type(arg)
       return arg

   return inner(arg)
   ```
   This approach is more explicit and avoids any potential side effects of the inner function.

### Conclusion

The key takeaway is that type narrowing in nested scopes isn't automatically inherited. By using an assertion or reassigning the variable, you can help the type checker understand the correct type in the inner function. This ensures that your code is both type-safe and compatible with static type checkers. If you have any more questions or need further clarification, feel free to ask! 😊

